<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lamu Old Town</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lamu Old Town is the historic centre of Lamu, on Lamu Island off the northern coast of Kenya. Inhabited for more than seven centuries, it is the oldest and best-preserved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, with narrow streets, coral-stone houses with carved wooden doors, and mosques. It was a major port of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a> and became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lamu-old-town.jpg" alt="Lamu Old Town" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Almaddy2022 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lamu_Old_Town.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
